	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Each companion type grants you a unique benefit.</p><p><strong>Acolyte:</strong> You gain proficiency in Religion and are able to make a DC 8 Persuasion check to receive lodging and a moderate lifestyle for up to a week at any friendly church, temple, or monastery.</p><p><strong>Construct:</strong> You gain proficiency in Engineering and the cost to repair or craft equipment is halved.</p><p><strong>Cultist:</strong> You gain proficiency in Insight and Deception.</p><p><strong>Fey:</strong> You gain proficiency in Nature and cannot become lost when traveling through forests, mountains, or plains.</p><p><strong>Hedge Wizard:</strong> You gain proficiency in Medicine and receive the maximum amount of healing when drinking common and uncommon Potions of Healing.</p><p><strong>Hunter:</strong> You gain proficiency in Survival and can go without Supply for a number of days equal to your Constitution modifier without gaining fatigue.</p><p><strong>Mage:</strong> You gain proficiency in Arcana and may cast Identify as a ritual.</p><p><strong>Scoundrel:</strong> You gain proficiency in Sleight of Hand and Stealth.</p><p><strong>Squire:</strong> You gain proficiency in History and can make a forced march for an additional number of hours equal to your Constitution modifier without gaining fatigue.</p><p><strong>Undead:</strong> You gain the Chill Touch and Spare the Dying cantrips.</p>",
